## The code

One group of four files, in two commits:

- Commit 34d37ffc: `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/card-kit.ts`,
  `dashboard/lib/storytime/print/pictures.ts`,
  `dashboard/scripts/storytime/check-storytime-pictures.ts`, and
  `dashboard/scripts/storytime/make-card-kit-pdf.ts`.
- Commit 1aa9d06d: `dashboard/scripts/storytime/make-card-kit-pdf.ts` only. The `PROJECT_CHECKS`
  gate gave the TypeScript error TS2451, because the build used the name `counts` twice. The
  commit gives the match counts their own name.

The changes:

- F20: `check-storytime-pictures.ts` requests the card rows of the requested weeks after the book
  rows. A card row of a week is requested when the batch holds a job for it, or when the batch
  holds no job for any row of that week. A batch that holds the book rows of a week holds no card
  row of that week, so its request stays the book rows. That rule keeps R-P4-28 and R-P8-F20
  both green. The rule was needed: an unconditional request makes R-P4-28 fail, because the
  week 1 batch of that test holds the 29 book rows and no card row.
- F21: the JSDoc of `STORYTIME_STICKER_CENTER_OVERRIDES` and of the option `centers` names the
  sticker label as the only key. No behavior change.
- F22: the new export `storytimeCardMatchCounts(lines)` counts the lines of the match report by
  source. The build prints `picture cards: 106, picture 57, patch 8, dots 9, none 32` and
  `distinct words: 94, picture 46, patch or dots 17, none 31`.
- F24: the patch markup carries `data-shape="rounded-rectangle"`. The look of the A6 file does
  not change, because the patch fills the same picture area.
- F25: `storytimeCardPictureRows` throws on a repeated word, and the message names the word. The
  compare ignores the case and holds in every week.
- F30: `storytimeDeliveredPictures(folder, rows)` is the new export of `card-kit.ts`, with the
  behavior and the JSDoc of the old private function of the build script. The build calls it.

