## The blocker

G-P8-M8 of the Red test file `__tests__/storytime-print-card-kit-match.test.ts` times out. The
test calls `shipped()`, which reads the shipped picture folder through
`resolveStorytimePictureFiles`. The folder holds 1235 MB of color files, and the SHA-256 of that
folder takes 5424 ms on this CPU (an Intel i5-3470S without SHA-NI, 211 to 244 MB/s). The
default vitest timeout is 5000 ms, so no Green can pass that test. The probe
`green-p8-r7-probe-timing.ts` holds that measurement, and `green-p8-r7-probe-hash.ts` holds the
hash speed of the CPU.

The sibling tests of the same file that call `shipped()` carry the timeout `120_000`, and the plan
line 1121 records the same fix for the sibling file in commit e7962b54. The Red test of this round
has no timeout, so it is a defect of the Red test, not of the code. This role changed no test
file.

The fix is one word in the Red test: `it('G-P8-M8 ...', async () => { ... }, 120_000);`. A Mid Red
retry makes that change. The next Green then runs the gates again and changes no code.

## The plan

The plan holds the six line corrections and one new sub-line, each with the marker
`[corrected in review round 4, F<n>]`, and the evidence of this round under the Green line. The
Green line stays `[~]`, because the targeted command and the two vitest gates exit 1 on the Red
test defect.

